145
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Ez emrê min pênc bûn yan şeş bûn, pênc bû ez hîn bûm.
 
I was five or six years old, I was five when I learned.

146
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Ez bi hêvî me gotinên te rast bin, pênc salî bû hînî tembûrê
bûye.
 
I hope your words are true, he learned the tanbur when he
was five years old.

147
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Ez jî nizanim tembûrê bixim.
 
Even I don't know how to play the tanbur.

148
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Hehe.
 
Hehe.

149
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Feyme, tu jî dizanî tenbûrê xî lê?
 
Feyme, do you also know how to play the tanbur?

150
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,000
Hinekî.
 
A little bit.

151
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Lê ne zêde.
 
But not much.

152
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Lê ez jî tenbûrê çep dixim.
 
But I play the tanbur left-handed.

153
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Çep?
 
Left-handed?

154
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Ez dixwazim te ji min re xeber de tu kengî hînî tembûrê, di
kîjan emrî da... te kê hîn kirî... kî te elimand?
 
Yes.

155
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Ez dixwazim te ji min re xeber de tu kengî hînî tembûrê, di
kîjan emrî da... te kê hîn kirî... kî te elimand?
 
I want you to tell me when you learned the tanbur, at what
age... who taught you... who instructed you?

156
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Wele, alîkariya dayîka min, bavê min, yanî wan ez elimandim.
 
Well, with the help of my mother and my father, I mean, they
taught me.

157
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:20,000
Û emrê min pênc bûn em li muxeyem bûn.
 
And I was five years old when we were in the camp.

158
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
Emrê min pênc bû ez milê xwe daxist.
 
I was five years old when I put my arm down (started
playing).

159
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:27,000
Hûn koçber bûn, hûn di çadirê da bûn... û li wê derê te hînî
tembûrê bûyî.
 
You were displaced, you were in a tent... and there you
learned the tanbur.

160
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

161
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Û bavê te û dayîka te jî te re bûn alîkar.
 
And your father and mother also helped you.

162
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
Erê û em gelek koçber bûn.
 
Yes, and we were displaced a lot.

163
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Hûn çend ciyan geriyan heta hûn hatin Efrînê?
 
How many places did you move around to before you came to
Afrin?

164
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Em ji Şehbayê... em ji Efrîn koçber bûn em çûn Şehbayê,
 
We went from Shahba... we were displaced from Afrin and went
to Shahba,

165
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
û ji Şehbayê jî em çûn Reqayê,
 
and from Shahba we went to Raqqa,

166
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
ji Reqayê em çûn Tebqayê, û ji Tebqayê em hatin Qamişloyê.
 
from Raqqa we went to Tabqa, and from Tabqa we came to
Qamishli.

167
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

168
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Feyme... ji dengbêjên me Efrîn, kîjanî kêlek we sekînî?
 
Feyme... among our Afrin singers, who stood by your side?

169
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Gava ku em stranê dibêjin, em klîba çêdikin,
 
When we sing songs, when we make clips,

170
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
kîjan stranbêj kêlek we sekînî?
 
which singer stood by your side?

171
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Ez dixwazim tu navên wan ji min ra xeber de.
 
I want you to tell me their names.

172
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Ez silavên xwe li te dikim. Mamoste Welat silavên xwe rêdike
ji te re.
 
I send my greetings to you. Teacher Welat sends you his
greetings.

173
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Spas ji mamoste Welat re.
 
Thanks to Teacher Welat.

174
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Xeynî mamoste Welat da te kes ji dengbêjên me yên Efrînê
pirs na...
 
Besides teacher Welat, hasn't anyone from our Afrin singers
asked...

175
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Em nikanin navê wan hildin bes ew ji te pirr in.
 
We can't name them, but they are numerous,

176
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Yanî te kesek din heye weha tu ji kê hez dikî?
 
I mean, is there anyone else you like?

177
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Piştî dengê wan ê xweş em klîpekê jî we re çêkin.
 
Because of their beautiful voices, we should make a clip for
you as well.

178
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Spas ji kedkariya te ya bi me re. Me klîp çêkir û mamoste
Welat Can jî me re... kelîme gotin.
 
Thanks for the effort you put in with us. We made a clip,
and teacher Welat Can also said a few words for us.

179
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Klîpeke din ê ku we çêkir min dît, ew li ser Newrozê ye.
 
The other clip you made that I saw, is about Newroz.

180
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

181
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Û te stranek welê negot ku we di klîbê de navê Efrînê...
Efrîn navê wê lê bikin...
 
And didn't you sing a song in the clip where you mentioned
Afrin... named Afrin...

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Erê, min afrînî got, û stran jî ez dimê... stranan jî ez
dibêjim.
 
Yes, I said 'Afrin' and the song is also mine... I sing the
songs.

183
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Ez dixwazim tiştekî ji we bipirsim, pir vîdyoyên we derbas
bûn l' cem me, tu qenatek te weha l' cem we heye, we nîşan
dabe mobayl?
 
I want to ask you something, many of your videos reached us,
do you have a channel, do you guys have mobile phones?

184
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Erê qenateke me YouTube heye, TikTok heye, hema Facebook...
 
Yes, we have a YouTube channel, TikTok, and Facebook...

185
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
In vîdeoyên xwe li wir datînin da xelk...
 
And you upload your videos there so people...

186
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
Erê l' ser Facebookê jî heye.
 
Yes, it is also on Facebook.

187
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Belê. Naha tu dengbêj î, me te tiştek ji me re amade kiriye?
 
Yes. Now that you are a singer, have you prepared something
for us?

188
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Te çi amade kiriye? Straneke dîtir?
 
Yes.

189
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,000
Te çi amade kiriye? Straneke dîtir?
 
What have you prepared? Another song?

190
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
Folklorê Efrîn.
 
Afrin folklore.

191
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
Te çi stran ji me re amade kiriye niha? A didu ye.
 
What song have you prepared for us now? The second one.

192
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Aw jî folklorê Efrîn e a dibêje: "Nanî nanî gulê zer"
 
That is also Afrin folklore, the one that goes "Nani Nani
Gule Zer."

193
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Nanî nanî gulazer.
 
Nani Nani Gulazer.

194
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:01,000
De niha em bi hev re guhdar bikin.
 
Yes.

195
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:14,000
De niha em bi hev re guhdar bikin.
 
So now let's listen to it together.

196
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Nanî nanî Gulazer, nanî nanî Gulazer.
 
Nani Nani Gulazer, Nani Nani Gulazer.

197
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Qurban dîmê te esmer, qurban dîmê te esmer.
 
I would sacrifice myself for your tanned face, I would
sacrifice myself for your tanned face.

198
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Dîmê tûtî gulave, dîmê tûtî gulave.
 
Your face is like a jar of rose water, your face is like a
jar of rose water.

199
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Mûş û banê pezî gav, mûş û banê pezî gav.
 
The fragrance of a flock of sheep, the fragrance of a flock
of sheep.

200
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Nanî nanî Gulazer, nanî nanî Gulazer.
 
Nani Nani Gulazer, Nani Nani Gulazer.

201
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:57,000
Meşle herakê çû me ba te, meşle herakê çû me ba te.
 
Walking step by step, I came to you, walking step by step, I
came to you.

202
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Dengê kermê ye qemer, dengê kermê ye qemer.
 
Hearing the brown sheep, hearing the brown sheep.

203
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:08,000
Hezar tucar hatiye ser, hezar tucar hatiye ser.
 
A thousand merchants came for her, a thousand merchants came
for her.

204
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Hezar weraqa daniye ser, hezar weraqa daniye ser.
 
They offered a thousand banknotes for her, they offered a
thousand banknotes for her.

205
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Nanî nanî Gulazer, nanî nanî Gulazer.
 
Nani Nani Gulazer, Nani Nani Gulazer.

206
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Min nefroşin bi qemer, min nefroşin bi qemer.
 
Don't sell me for gold coins, don't sell me for gold coins.

207
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Dadêna, gulê dîn e, dadêna, gulê dîn e.
 
The mother is crazy, Gule is crazy, the mother is crazy,
Gule is crazy.

208
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Fîstanê gulê rengîn e, fîstanê gulê rengîn e.
 
Gule's dress is colorful, Gule's dress is colorful.

209
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Bi ser malê de, rêt xwîn e, bi ser malê de, rêt xwîn e.
 
Blood was spilled over the house, blood was spilled over the
house.

210
00:12:55,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Teyr bi ser malê rêt xwîn e, teyr bi ser malê rêt xwîn e.
 
The bird over the house spilled blood, the bird over the
house spilled blood.

211
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Nanî nanî Gulazer, nanî nanî Gulazer.
 
Nani Nani Gulazer, Nani Nani Gulazer.

212
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Xeber ji gulê re hat, xeber ji gulê re hat.
 
News came to Gule, news came to Gule.

213
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Fîstanê gulê dizîn e, fîstanê gulê dizîn e.
 
They stole Gule's dress, they stole Gule's dress.

214
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Her du destan li xwe dixîne, her du destan li xwe dixîne.
 
She beats herself with both hands, she beats herself with
both hands.

215
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Nanî nanî Gulazer, nanî nanî Gulazer.
 
Nani Nani Gulazer, Nani Nani Gulazer.

216
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Dengê te sax be. Bi rastî ez pir kêfxweş bûm, min
naskirin...
 
May your voice be healthy (God bless your voice). Truly, I
am very happy, I met you...

217
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Pir kes wê jî pir kêfxweş bibin, gava em xortekî me
weciwan...
 
Many people will also be very happy, when we see a young boy
like you...

218
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:51,000
dengê wî te wisa pir xweş dibînin...
 
with such a very beautiful voice...

219
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Gava yek ji te re dibêje dengê te xweş e, tu kêf dikî?
 
When someone tells you that your voice is beautiful, do you
get happy?

220
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

221
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
Kêfa te tê ye?
 
Does it make you happy?

222
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,000
İnşallah rojên pêş de em ê pir klîbên baştir amade bikin.
 
Hopefully in the coming days, we will prepare much better
clips.

223
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Ev strana niha te gotî "Gulazer" ev ya kê ye?
 
This song you just sang, "Gulazer", whose is it?

224
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Ev folklorê Efrînê ye, ê mamoste Hesen Evdo ye.
 
This is the folklore of Afrin, by teacher Hesen Evdo.

225
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Belê, va stranên folklorê me yê Efrînê ne, ê mamoste Hesen
Evdo ne.
 
Yes, these are the folklore songs of our Afrin, by teacher
Hesen Evdo.

226
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Çima te ev stran... hilbijart ku tu bêjî?
 
Why did you choose this song to sing?

227
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Ji ber folklorê Efrînê ye, yanî xweş e.
 
Because it's Afrin's folklore, meaning it's beautiful.

228
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Te got ez hez jê dikim?
 
You said you like it?

229
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Erê. Kêfa min têyê.
 
Yes. I enjoy it.

230
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Ez dixwazim Fehîm... ez ji te jî bipirsim tiştekî, hûn
dixwînin dibistanê de? L' te dev jê berdaye weha?
 
I want to ask Fehim... I want to ask you something too, do
you study in school? Or did you drop out?

231
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Erê rast hema me dev jê berdaye.
 
Yes, truly we just dropped out.

232
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Hûn naçin hema... hûn neçûyîn?
 
You just don't go... you didn't go?

233
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Na, em heta, di muxeyemê da jî em neçûyîn.
 
No, we haven't gone since we've been in the camp.

234
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,000
Tu çendê dixwînî?
 
What grade are you in?

235
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Ew dî heştan da ye ev... em dî pêncan da ye.
 
He is in eighth grade, and I... we are in fifth.

236
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Û ew xwendin ma ji wî... dev jê nabe ne ku we mekteb
berdaye?
 
And did you stop your education there... did you drop out of
school?

237
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Mamoste em nizanin... em Kurmancî dizanin em... Erebî kêm
dizanin, tiştan kêm dizanin. Erebî em nizanin deng biken
jî... hema nizanin.
 
The teachers don't know... we know Kurmanji but... we know
very little Arabic, we know little about those things. We
don't even know how to speak Arabic.

238
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Ê li wî derê mamoste we Erebî bûn...
 
So the teachers there speak Arabic...

239
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Erebî nizanin...
 
They don't know Arabic...

240
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,000
hûn bi zimanê Erebî baş nizanin... hûn mecbûr we xwendin
berdaye.
 
You don't know the Arabic language well... you were forced
to drop out.

241
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Em Erebî nizanin deng biken gava çawa we... hîn bibin.
 
We don't know how to speak Arabic, how are we supposed to...
learn.

242
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
Yanî li cem we gava li Kurdî bixwînin wê baştir be...
 
So for you, if you studied in Kurdish, it would be better...

243
00:14:53,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Erê! Hema em Kurdî dizanin bixwînin em dizanin binivîsin, em
dizanin her tiştî.
 
Yes! We know how to read in Kurdish, we know how to write,
we know everything.

244
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Ev kilama we jî... we jî wekî kilam ji me re hazir kiriye?
Am pê kêfxweş dibin.
 
Have you prepared a song for us as well? We would be happy.

245
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Heya kilama Sisiye ew jî em ê diyariyî miletê Efrînê bikin.
 
We have the song of Sisiye, we will gift it to the people of
Afrin as well.

246
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:32,000
Am niha bi hev re guhdar dikin.
 
We will listen to it together now.

247
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Min te dîtibû li ser bîrê lê lê, ser bîrê.
 
I had seen you at the well, oh, at the well.

248
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Av dikişandî bi zencîrê.
 
You were drawing water with a chain.

249
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Radimîsim keça pîrê.
 
I kiss the old woman's daughter.

250
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Way lê lê, way lê lê, malê wêran.
 
Oh dear, oh dear, ruined home.

251
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Diçûme mala, çûm ba wê.
 
I went to the house, I went to her.

252
00:15:56,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Çavreşê gerdinxweşê.
 
Black-eyed, beautiful-necked.

253
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Min te dîtibû nav tûtûnê, nav tûtûnê.
 
I had seen you among the tobacco, among the tobacco.

254
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Agir danî ser qelûnê.
 
You put fire on the pipe.

255
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Radimîsim keça xatûnê.
 
I kiss the lady's daughter.

256
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Way lê lê, way lê lê, malê wêran.
 
Oh dear, oh dear, ruined home.

257
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Diçûme mala, çûm ba wê.
 
I went to the house, I went to her.

258
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Çavreşê gerdinxweşê.
 
Black-eyed, beautiful-necked.

259
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Min te dîtibû nav keleka, nav keleka.
 
I had seen you on the raft, on the raft.

260
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Keçê meke wan heneka.
 
Girl, don't make those jokes.

261
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Way lê lê, way lê lê, malê wêran.
 
Oh dear, oh dear, ruined home.

262
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Diçûme mala, çûm ba wê.
 
I went to the house, I went to her.

263
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Çavreşê gerdinxweşê.
 
Black-eyed, beautiful-necked.

264
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:24,000
Dengê we sax be, bi rastî ez pir kêfxweş bûm, û rojbaş wek
te min nas kir wexta me gellek bi hev ra dît.
 
Bless your voices, I was truly very happy, and good day to
you as we met each other like this.

265
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Navî te pir xweş e. Tu wilo ne xeyîdî xuya dikî lê dîsa xweş
e jî.
 
Your name is very beautiful. You look a little sullen, but
it's fine.

266
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Û stranên te gotin jî pir xweş bûn, am... ji wan...
 
And the songs you sang were very beautiful, we...

267
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Am silavên xwe dişînin ji xwedanê van stranan re.
 
We send our greetings to the owners of these songs.

268
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Van stranan, kî van stranan, ew wextê ew stranan tu dengê
wan digirî û tu ji ber wan dixwînî, we ha hûn guhdar dikin
ew te kîşan weha dîtibû we ew girt û hîn bûn we bi xwe.
 
These songs, how do you learn these songs when you hear
them, who showed them to you that you listened to and
learned on your own?

269
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Klîban em bixwe bixwe li vîdyoyê didin... em didin em dawe
didin li ser YouTube-ê...
 
We ourselves post videos... we post them on YouTube...

270
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Ewe li telefonê da didin nav l' ser YouTube...
 
You post them from your phone to YouTube...

271
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Em ta'lîqatan dixwînin, ê dinivîsin li pêş vîdeoyan.
 
We read the comments they write on the videos.

272
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Kê şîyar we... ta'lîqatan nivîsîn?
 
Who writes the comments?

273
00:17:53,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Erê. Bawer ke dinivîsin wekî wê... navê wê dinivîsin, êdî em
dibînin em bixwe jî daxwazên wan didin, em wan kilaman
çêdikin am a pir hatî xwestin, me jî da we...
 
Yes. Believe me, they write the names of the songs, so we
see their requests, and the song that is requested the most,
we...

274
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Yanî ew yekî heye we ku ta'lîqat tê daxwaz ji we dîtin?
 
I see, so there is someone who writes comments and requests
it from you?

275
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Belê her yek.
 
Yes, everyone.

276
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Yanî me we wek... wê xwest, hûn stranê derdixînin daxwaz...
 
I mean, they request it, and you release the song for
them...

277
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Mesela em kilama bixwe li telefonê hîn dibin... mesele me
yek kilam weha ji me xwest.
 
For instance, we learn the song ourselves on the phone...
for example, someone requests a song from us.

278
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Çend rojan dikişîne heta hûn stranekê digrin, jê hifz dikin,
paşê tu wê bêjî?
 
How many days does it take for you to pick up a song,
memorize it, and then sing it?

279
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:35,000
Bavo meselen em stranek wek wilo hûn dibêjin am hez dikin em
diçin YouTube em em derdixin em guhdar dikin. Am am sê caran
am guhdar dikin em hîn dibin, wilo am hez diki ew ji hew dû
sê rojan am am hazir dikin.
 
Man, for example, if we hear a song and we like it, we go to
YouTube and listen to it. We listen to it three times and we
learn it, and we prepare it in two or three days.

280
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Heta we kilamek derdixistin ev dema tu stranek din ji nû
digirî, pêwist e hûn fêr bikin bixwe li ser defterekî?
 
When you get a song or when you want to learn a new one, do
you have to write it down in a notebook?

281
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Erê... deftara em l' pêş me ye em dinivîsin lê.
 
Yes... we have a notebook in front of us and we write on it.

282
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,000
Defterekî l' cem we stranan l' ser dinivîsin, weha?
 
You have a notebook where you write the songs?

283
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:51,000
Erê am wê dinivîsin e, qe me ji bîr nekir. Qet qe ma ji bîr
kir, em deftara...
 
Yes, we write it down so we don't forget. In case we forget,
we have the notebook...

284
00:18:51,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Em pê dizanin e. Em wê weke l' ser dinivîsin, tiştê we ji
bîr kir, hûn cardî dinêrin ew li wira dîsa tu we hazir dike
û... hûn hîn dibin.
 
I see. You write it down, and if you forget, you look at it
again, prepare it, and learn it.

285
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:07,000
We çiqas we stranan jê girt em dîsa wisa jê dizanin we.
 
No matter how many songs we learn, we know them like that.

286
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Dengê we pir xweş e, gelek spas ji te re Rojvan...
 
Your voice is very beautiful, thank you very much Rojvan.

287
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Stranek bi te jî hez kiriye zêde we te kîjan e?
 
Which song is the one you like the most?

288
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Kîjan kilam e me... me weha...
 
Which song...

289
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Reşê e.
 
It's 'Reşê'.

290
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Av a niha, te ji te re Reşê kîjan... Reşê? E.
 
Now, which 'Reşê' for you... 'Reşê'? Yes.

291
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Bêguman am a vê stranê guhdar bikin. Lê berî strana we ez
bidim dest pê kirin... fehîma bavo ez xwazim e.. te û birayê
te Rojvan. Xûşkek jî mufîde jî... wî stran we digot. Am
silavan li mufîde ra jî daxwazî. Ee we di nav vî tiştî da
guhdar dikin kê, hûn ê kê zêde dibîhîzin, dengbêjên we efrîn
hûn j' kê hez dikin bêtir bêtir.. as?
 
Of course we will listen to this song. But before I start
your song... Fehim man, I want to... you and your brother
Rojvan. You also have a sister named Mufide... she used to
sing with you. We send our greetings to Mufide too. Whom do
you listen to, whom do you follow... which of our Afrin
singers do you like the most?

292
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:49,000
E... ez gelek ê... ji Alî Teço hez dikim...
 
I... I like Ali Teço a lot...

293
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Tu weke li dengê Alî Teço e.. hez dikî hûn.. e.
 
You like the voice of Ali Teço.

294
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Ew jî... ê hez dikim da. Ew zêde stranê wan zêde xweş e.
 
Yes... I like it. Most of their songs are very beautiful.

295
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Gistî stranên wî giran in pir pir pir kevin in.
 
Almost all of his songs are heavy and very, very old.

296
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Ev Fehîm e. Te hunermendê me, te gel kê anîye?
 
Very old...

297
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Ev Fehîm e. Te hunermendê me, te gel kê anîye?
 
This is Fehim. Who did you bring our artist with?

298
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Mamo, ew pismamê min Rojan e, tu nas dikî.
 
Uncle, he is my cousin Rojan, you know him.

299
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
